# Build context excludes for every Containerfile in deploy/podman/ that
# uses `workspace/bahyway_v4` as its build context (`COPY . .`).
#
# FIXED (2026-07-27): no .containerignore existed here at all, so every
# `podman build` COPYing this directory transferred the ENTIRE workspace
# including `target/` -- 21G in a real, cargo-built checkout (measured
# live) -- into the build layer. Confirmed live on eriduous-vdi: a real
# `podman build -f deploy/podman/Containerfile.asset-server` ran for 28
# real minutes and then failed at the `COPY . .` step with `no space
# left on device` writing to `/var/tmp` -- committing that oversized
# layer exhausted host disk space. `target/` is rebuilt fresh inside the
# container by `cargo build --release` anyway (see the Containerfile's
# own builder stage), so copying the host's own already-built artifacts
# in was never useful, only expensive.
target/
**/target/
.git/
**/.godot/
